meta {
  name: Impersonate - View a role route as a user (X-Impersonate-User)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/manager/shifts?month=2026-07
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{web_admin_token}}
}

headers {
  X-Impersonate-User: {{user_id}}
}

docs {
  Acting as a user is a header on the ORDINARY role route — there is no impersonate-prefixed
  path. Authenticate as a WebAdmin (web_admin_token) and set `X-Impersonate-User` to the target's
  Cognito sub; the response is exactly what `GET /manager/shifts` returns for that manager.

  Every employee / manager / org-admin route accepts the header (see `ImpersonationHeader` in
  contracts/src/schemas/common.ts). Resolved by `withImpersonation` in each role Lambda
  (backend/src/functions/shared/impersonation.ts).

  Errors, in the order they are checked:
    403 - caller is not a provisioned, ACTIVE WebAdmin (also for any other role sending the header)
    403 - any method other than GET — impersonation sessions are read-only
    400 - `X-Impersonate-User` is not a valid id
    400 - the route is not a role route (e.g. /web-admin/..., /health)
    404 - the id is not a member of the role this route serves
          (e.g. an Employee id sent to /manager/shifts)
}
